    "q-171685": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171685",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of positive integers between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive: \n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x$ is prime",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P},\n$$\n\nThe truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of primes between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{2,3,5,7\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{\\{2,3,5,7\\}} \\\\  & =\\{1,4,6,8,9,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
