    "q-175518": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175518",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-7<-9$",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & <-9 \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-2).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{(-\\infty ,-2)} \\\\  & =[-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
